table([['Diagnostic','Result'],['Original singlet norm',str(r['original_color']['norm'])],['Maximum total-generator action','0 in the recorded floating-point run'],['Generator Gram-matrix error',f"{e['gram_error']:.3e}"],['Commutator-closure residual',f"{e['commutator_closure_error']:.3e}"],['Common kernel dimension','1, numerical and exact symbolic'],['Collective SU(3) rotation residual (32 trials)',f"{e['collective_SU3_rotation_max_error_32_cases']:.3e}"],['Joint-state projection/factorization error',f"{e['projected_joint_state_factorization_error']:.3e}"],['Product rgb state: maximum total-charge norm',f"{e['basis_rgb_total_charge_max_norm']:.9f}"],['One-site phase error: maximum total-charge norm',f"{e['one_site_phase_error_total_charge_max_norm']:.9f}"]],[300,175])
p('The negative controls deliberately violate the singlet contract and are detected. They show that the tests can reject specific non-singlet states, rather than returning zero for every input. Exact symbolic nullspace calculation uses nonzero rescalings of the eight generators to eliminate square roots; this preserves the common kernel and verifies the signed integer singlet vector without floating-point tolerance. The factorization diagnostic projects a seeded arbitrary 6-address by 27-color positive density operator onto the singlet sector, normalizes it, and compares it with the tensor product of its address marginal and the fixed singlet projector.')
p('The 36 checks are grouped by purpose: five finite-source/assembly checks; fifteen comparisons with frozen component outputs; one exact charge-motif check; nine generator, kernel, rotation and reduced-state checks; two symmetry-breaking negative controls; three exact-kernel/factorization checks; and one source-hash check. Several test related identities or replay the same source, so the count is a test-suite status rather than 36 independent pieces of scientific evidence.')
