p('audit_results.json records the runtime versions, thresholds, inputs, declared checks and full output values. SOURCE_SHA256.json is verified before execution and is not overwritten; a changed or missing source makes execution fail. Rerunning writes audit_results.json, and differing numerical-library versions or runtime metadata may change its file hash. Preserve the distributed reference output when checking release hashes and use the recorded tolerances for numerical comparisons. The scientific calculation is separate from PDF rendering.')
p('Exact audit release: WRRA-COLOR-AUDIT-20261020-v0.5. RELEASE.json supplies the release identifier, upstream commit and content SHA-256 identifiers for the final manuscript, executable audit, frozen-source manifest and results. This versioned, content-addressed package distinguishes the new audit from its upstream sources. The unchanged scientific audit.py, frozen source/ inputs and reference audit_results.json are publicly archived at <link href="https://github.com/Wonsik-Choi-janefather/wrra-m-0.1/tree/3e8f1b7cb183aba8af14a7e435d5e339e63c5ab1/publication/WRRA_Schwartz_Contract_Audit_v1_2" color="blue">permanent GitHub code commit 3e8f1b7cb183aba8af14a7e435d5e339e63c5ab1</link>. Download that repository commit and run from publication/WRRA_Schwartz_Contract_Audit_v1_2. The earlier v0.3 color manuscript and complete audit package are also archived at DOI 10.5281/zenodo.23495570. These existing archives supply the unchanged calculation; they do not identify this revised v0.5 PDF. The exact v0.5 manuscript, scripts, frozen inputs, results and RELEASE.json are in the <link href="https://github.com/Wonsik-Choi-janefather/wrra-m-0.1/tree/main/publication/WRRA_Color_Interface_Audit_v0_5" color="blue">versioned v0.5 public archive</link>. RELEASE.json identifies this final PDF by SHA-256; README.txt supplies its immutable archive commit. The earlier archive remains provenance for v0.3. This revision adds the dependency check and the explicit failed-decoder example within the same particle/color scope; no other physical model is substituted.')
p('A passed software check does not establish observational agreement. Known values used as inputs and their reproduction remain legitimate disclosed model construction and consistency results. No independent prediction is required to recognize that contribution; equally, the present tests cannot support a claim that the unimplemented arithmetic-to-color selection has already been calculated.')
p('<b>Conclusion.</b> The WRRA component replay is reproducible under its frozen inputs and its supplied color-singlet contract. The exact rank-one color sector imposes a concrete interface restriction: it carries no independent address-color correlations. A future arithmetic color mechanism must explicitly overcome that restriction through a stated extension. This is a targeted audit and model-development result; publication suitability is left to independent review.')
